        },
        {
          "text": "For each component, initial_split subtracts accumulated persistent bytes and the maximum temporary charge seen so far from each device's working budget and clips the result at zero. If every weight is zero, it retries with each working budget multiplied by 11/10 and rounded down in bytes. It does this before masking devices: limit 1 keeps only slot 0; other non-None limits still keep the slots with the most remaining room. ratio_split floors proportional quotas in indivisible allocation units and distributes leftovers by largest fractional remainder. Replicated charges depend on the positive-weight mask, not the rounded split. Split charges are prorated; only overhead_to_split gets the forward-token multiplier, with output_num_tokens used for the final component. Persistent costs sum across components; temporary costs take a per-device maximum. The new report shows the two terms and their sum, with a 1024³ divisor despite the GB label.",
